1. Definitions

"Software" means the ConTP software, including its source code,
documentation, associated files, and any modifications or derivative
works thereof made available under this License.

"Permitted Research Use" means use of the Software for academic,
scientific, educational, evaluation, or internal research purposes,
provided that the Software is not used as part of a commercial
product, paid service, or commercial deployment.

Permitted Research Use may be conducted by individuals, universities,
academic institutions, non-profit organizations, research institutes,
or commercial entities. The commercial or non-commercial status of
the user or organization alone does not determine whether a use is
permitted under this License.

"Commercial Use" means use of the Software, directly or indirectly,
as part of a product, service, deployment, or other activity that is
offered commercially or generates revenue, or is intended to provide
a commercial product or service to customers or other third parties.

2. Permission for Research Use

Subject to the terms and conditions of this License, the copyright
holder grants you a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free,
non-transferable license to use, reproduce, and modify the Software
for Permitted Research Use.

Permitted Research Use includes, but is not limited to:

(a) academic and scientific research at universities and research
    institutions;

(b) teaching and educational use;

(c) research and evaluation by non-profit organizations;

(d) internal research, testing, benchmarking, and evaluation by
    commercial companies, provided that such use does not constitute
    Commercial Use as defined in Section 4; and

(e) reproduction of research results and evaluation of the Software
    for scientific purposes.

No separate permission from the copyright holder is required for
Permitted Research Use.

