4. Commercial Use

Commercial Use of the Software is NOT permitted under this License
without prior written authorization from the copyright holder.

Commercial Use includes, but is not limited to:

(a) incorporating the Software, in whole or in part, into a commercial
    product;

(b) incorporating the Software into a paid or revenue-generating
    service;

(c) offering functionality based on the Software to customers or
    third parties as part of a paid product or service;

(d) deploying the Software as part of a commercial production system
    or commercial customer-facing system;

(e) selling, sublicensing, or commercially distributing the Software
    or a derivative work; or

(f) using the Software to provide paid consulting, analysis,
    computation, software-as-a-service, or other services to third
    parties.

For clarity, use of the Software by a for-profit company solely for
internal research, experimentation, testing, benchmarking, or
evaluation is considered Permitted Research Use and does NOT, by
itself, constitute Commercial Use.

However, if the Software or a derivative work is subsequently
incorporated into, deployed as part of, or used to provide a
commercial product or paid service, prior written authorization and
a separate commercial license are required.

